{
  "requirement": "Configure the domain’s project files with {cite}`requirements.sdk.validation-cache.with_sources`. `Domain::project_sources` binds those files to the domain for Rust searches and agent inspection. Each hit identifies a node under {cite}`requirements.sdk.sources.source_nodes`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligations derived from `requirements.sdk.sources.provider.attachment`**\n1. Project files configured with `with_sources` are bound to the domain by `Domain::project_sources`. When no sources are configured, nothing is bound.\n2. The bound sources are used for Rust searches and for agent inspection.\n3. Each search hit identifies a node under `requirements.sdk.sources.source_nodes`.\n\nThe `with_sources` and `source_nodes` requirements are cited context. I did not reassess their own tests.\n\n**Implementation fact I checked**\n`Domain::project_sources` (`crates/trust-but-verify/src/domain.rs#trait[Domain]/fn[project_sources]`) returns `None` unless the cache has sources. Otherwise it returns a `SourceProject` that holds those sources and a clone of the domain. `SourceProject::search_text` and `search_structure` in `sources/hits.rs` intern each hit through `Domain::source_node`.\n\n**Test mapping**\n- **Obligation 1, absent case.** `tests/contracts.rs#fn[domain_without_project_sources_leaves_source_tools_disabled]` asserts that `project_sources()` is `None` and that `source_address` returns `None` for a domain with no sources.\n- **Obligation 1, configured case, and obligation 2.** `agent/configured.rs#mod[tests]/fn[configured_agent_uses_domain_source_tools_in_independent_executions]` builds the cache with `.with_sources(Sources::new(dir))`.\n  - `ConfiguredAgent::run` reaches the sources through `project_sources()`, so the test reaches the attachment end to end.\n  - The test asserts that the tool set includes `list_sources`, `outline_source`, `search_text`, `search_structure` and `finish_search`.\n  - It calls `list_sources`, `read_node`, and `search_text` over the attached directory, in two independent runs.\n  - It asserts that `.gitignore`d and out-of-scope files are not exposed.\n- **Obligation 3.** The same test asserts the following:\n  - Every `list_sources` entry has an integer `node` and an integer `data.id` from the domain's `NodeData`.\n  - `read_node` on a hit's `node` returns the mapped snapshot.\n  - The recorded dependencies are the domain nodes with ids 8, 9 and 10, each with the expected outline-content fingerprint.\n  - The domain's `source_node` calls are recorded as exactly the selected item, `visible/selected.txt`.\n  \n  Together these show that hits are interned in this domain's cache as nodes mapped under `source_nodes`.\n- **Domain binding and the unmapped-hit case.** The dependency assertions show hits resolving to this domain's nodes, so the domain is bound. `an_unmapped_hit_fails_the_search` in `agent/project_sources.rs` is marked for another requirement (`requirements.sdk.graph.search.domain_node`).\n- `supplied_openai_backend_runs_independent_calls_against_a_local_transport` carries the `{test}` reference but does not use `with_sources`. It adds nothing here, and nothing depends on it.\n\n**Possible gaps considered**\n- No test calls `domain.project_sources().unwrap().search_structure(...)` through a domain-attached project. The `agent/project_sources.rs` tests build the project through the `ProjectSources::new` helper instead. Text search through the attachment is covered. Text and structural search share `find_hits` and the same domain interning. The requirement does not distinguish them, so a separate attachment test for each is not required.\n- The `None` and `Some` outcomes of `project_sources` are each asserted. The only conditional in that function is the `?` on the cache's `sources` field.\n\nI found no requirement-violating behavior that these tests would accept, so the tests adequately check the requirement. No `{fixme}` acknowledgments apply.",
  "references": "6c8ce8157893ac62f7994d2ab6e8b2ce8aea5bbb38571d10c5ffa8d4eb885fad",
